Now I understand the fuzzer. Let me focus on Stage 3. In Stage 3, the input is used as a default value in the schema:

```cpp
auto def_schema = "table X { Y: " + std::string(ref_res.type) + " = " +
                  input + "; } root_type X;" +
                  "{}";  // <- with empty json {}!
```

So the schema is `table X { Y: <type> = <input>; } root_type X;{}`.

Then `GenerateText` is called on `def_parser`. In `GenerateText`, `GenField` is called which calls `GetFieldDefault<T>(fd)`:

```cpp
template<typename T> static T GetFieldDefault(const FieldDef &fd) {
    T val;
    auto check = StringToNumber(fd.value.constant.c_str(), &val);
    (void)check;
    FLATBUFFERS_ASSERT(check);
    return val;
}
```

`fd.value.constant` is the default value string, which is the input. `StringToNumber` is called. If it fails, `val` is set to 0. But `FLATBUFFERS_ASSERT(check)` would fail.

Wait, but the issue is "Use-of-uninitialized-value". Let me look at `StringToNumber` for `bool`:

